# PaperTree: the environment for the three server processes (API, worker, agent).
#
#   cp .env.example .env
#   echo "PAPERTREE_AGENT_SECRET=$(openssl rand -hex 32)" >> .env
#   set -a; source .env; set +a       # in each terminal that starts the API, the worker or the agent
#
# The list is exactly research/build/reader-release/contracts.md section 7 (plus the agent's model
# policy, ADR-003). No process reads .env by itself: you export it. The web app has its own file
# (apps/web/.env.example).
#
# Lines that are not commented out are the defaults you would get anyway. Commented lines are
# optional. There is NO key in this file on purpose: PAPERTREE_MINIMAX_API_KEY goes to the agent
# process alone (see the README, "Quick start", terminal 3).

# --- api and worker ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# api, worker: SQLite plus uploads/ assets/ staging/. The API and the worker MUST share it.
PAPERTREE_DATA_ROOT=$HOME/.papertree
# api: where it listens.
PAPERTREE_HOST=127.0.0.1
PAPERTREE_PORT=8000
# api: where it reaches the agent.
PAPERTREE_AGENT_URL=http://127.0.0.1:8200
# api: login lifetime in hours (default 24).
# PAPERTREE_SESSION_HOURS=24
# api: largest accepted PDF upload, in MB (default 100).
# PAPERTREE_MAX_UPLOAD_MB=100
# api: HMAC key for asset URLs (default: random per boot, so asset URLs die with a restart).
# PAPERTREE_SIGNING_SECRET=
# api: per-user AI spend cap over a rolling 24 h, in USD (default 1.00), from ai_runs.cost_usd_est.
# PAPERTREE_DAILY_BUDGET_USD=1.00
# api: extra browser origins allowed beyond http://localhost:* and http://127.0.0.1:* (default none).
# PAPERTREE_CORS_ORIGINS=

# --- api and agent ----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# api, agent: the shared secret. REQUIRED for AI: without it the API answers 503 not_configured
# and the agent refuses to boot. The quick start appends it to .env (the `echo` above).
# PAPERTREE_AGENT_SECRET=

# --- agent ------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
# agent: its port (binds 127.0.0.1 only).
PAPERTREE_AGENT_PORT=8200
# agent: the API origin it fetches paper tools from (a run's tool URL must be on this origin).
PAPERTREE_API_INTERNAL_URL=http://127.0.0.1:8000
# agent: model policy (ADR-003). Defaults: explain and ask = MiniMax-M3.1-Flash-Preview at effort
# low, summary = MiniMax-M3. Set PAPERTREE_MODEL=MiniMax-M3 to put every kind back on M3.
# PAPERTREE_MODEL=
# PAPERTREE_MODEL_EXPLAIN=
# PAPERTREE_MODEL_ASK=
# PAPERTREE_MODEL_SUMMARY=
# agent: Flash only: low, medium or high (default low). Ignored for M3.
# PAPERTREE_MODEL_EFFORT=low
# PAPERTREE_MODEL_EFFORT_EXPLAIN=
# PAPERTREE_MODEL_EFFORT_ASK=
# PAPERTREE_MODEL_EFFORT_SUMMARY=
# agent: info (default) or debug (adds raw provider error text; never keys or tokens).
# PAPERTREE_AGENT_LOG_LEVEL=info
# agent: 1 = a scripted test model instead of MiniMax (the key is not read). Tests only; its
# answers are canned.
# PAPERTREE_AGENT_FAUX=

# PAPERTREE_MINIMAX_API_KEY  agent ONLY, required unless faux. Do not put it here: this file is
#                            sourced into the API and the worker too. Never use MINIMAX_API_KEY.
# PI_OFFLINE, PI_TELEMETRY, PI_CODING_AGENT_DIR: set by the agent itself at boot. Do not set them.
